      "id": 1,
      "text": "Cressey grew from a late‑19th‑century railway stop named for pioneer farmer George Cressey, with a post office opening in 1882.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cressey_california",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The arrival of the Central Pacific line turned the area into a farming hub, linking crops to markets.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cressey_california",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The post office opened in 1882, closed in 1883, reopened in 1909, and was renamed Cressey in 1912.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cressey%2C_California",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Cressey enjoys a Mediterranean climate with hot, dry summers and mild, wet winters typical of the Central Valley.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/cressey_california",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "other"
    },
    {
